lisa-design:
- Bootstrap image: alpine:3.21 + `apk add curl jq` at start when either is missing (same pattern as the chart's generate-public-key init container), so the default uses an official, small base image; any image that ships curl and jq skips apk (air-gapped clusters). Rejected: third-party curl+jq images (supply chain) and alpine/k8s (large).
- The Job runs as root by default (apk), with allowPrivilegeEscalation=false, drop ALL and seccomp RuntimeDefault; apk add verified to work with all capabilities dropped and no-new-privileges.
- Secrets go to the Kubernetes API with curl from the SA token, not kubectl. Role per target namespace: get limited to the configured Secret names, create unrestricted (RBAC cannot scope create by name).
- Idempotency: an existing Secret skips the agent (the client-secret cannot be read back). If Secret creation fails after a key was created, the key is revoked (DELETE /api/admin/agents/{id}/keys/{keyId}).
- No secret in argv or logs: request bodies via files (--data-binary @file), Authorization headers via -H @file, admin login via jq env.*; only non-2xx bodies are logged.
- Created Secrets are not Helm-managed (no ownership), so helm uninstall keeps working credentials.
